note right of "ores::iam::repository::account_repository"
The account table is the one repository with reads no other has:
read_any_by_username and read_latest_by_username/email. History is
addressed by the model key (the username) and must stay readable after a
delete, which closes the transaction-time window rather than removing
the row; a latest read cannot resolve a closed row, so read_any_by_username
ignores the window. check_service_credentials answers a uuid for the
service-login path, where the caller has a password but no session yet.
end note

