note right of "ores::iam::service::account_operations_service"
Hand-written. Passwords are hashed with ores.security's scrypt
password_hasher -- create_account hashes, login verifies -- and the
password columns never hold a plaintext value. login() refuses a
non-user account type and a locked account, increments failed_logins on
a bad password, and locks the account at five failed attempts. unlock()
clears both the lock and the counter; a successful login resets the
counter, stamps last_ip and last_login, and marks the account online.
create_service_account refuses a "user" type, because a service account
authenticates without a password.
end note

