note right of "ores::iam::service::cache::party_cache"
A partitioned, tenant-keyed cache of ores.refdata parties and the
party hierarchy. compute_visible_party_ids walks the cached children map
from a root party, which is how login, auth_event recording and internal
impersonation all resolve "the parties this account may see". load()
issues read_parties_for_cache over NATS, which needs a signed JWT, so the
cache is useless until set_token_provider arms it with a service token.
Copy and move are deleted: handlers share one instance through a
shared_ptr.
end note

