}
note right of "ores::iam::service::cache::warm_and_subscribe_party_cache"
An inline free function in party_cache_registrar.hpp. It warms each
tenant's partition, then subscribes to the party created, updated and
deleted event subjects; a mutation reloads the affected partition on a
detached thread, because load() blocks on request_sync and would
otherwise stall the NATS callback thread. A warm-up failure is logged
and does not fail startup.
end note

