note right of "ores::iam::messaging::auth_handler"
The largest hand-written handler and the one that mints tokens. signup
delegates to signup_service; login verifies the scrypt password through
account_operations_service, resolves the account's parties from
party_cache, and mints either an access token or -- when more than one
party is visible -- a short party-selection token. public_key answers the
verification key. refresh validates the signature even when the token is
expired, refuses once the session reaches max_session_s (recording a
max_session_exceeded audit event), and re-mints. service_login serves the
no-password service-account path through service_session_service. The
record_auth_event helper is the single place login, logout, refresh and
signup outcomes reach auth_event_repository.
end note

