note right of "ores::iam::messaging::tenant_provisioning_handler"
The Acme holding-group orchestrator, the first consumer of internal
actor impersonation. Rather than calling services in process -- which
would bypass the authorization, validation and audit trail a real
request goes through -- it mints one token per impersonated identity and
drives the real NATS pipeline through internal_request_client, hitting
refdata, dq and synthetic subjects as each party in turn. It holds no
repository. It is hand-written and not exposed as generated CRUD; the
two commands are wired by the registrar beside it.
end note

