class ores::iam::messaging::registrar {
    {static} +register_handlers(nats : client&, ctx : context, signer : jwt_authenticator, service_password : string) : vector<subscription>
}
note right of "ores::iam::messaging::registrar"
The component seam. register_handlers runs in two phases. Phase 1
constructs and subscribes every handler -- including service-login and
the generated registrars -- so every subject is answerable before
anything is called. Phase 2 then mints a service token through the
service account password, arms party_cache with it, reads every active
tenant through the unfiltered tenant_lookups and warms the cache, and
registers the seven per-entity history providers into one dispatch
registry behind the generic history.v1.get subject. It also wires the
variability system_setting_changed event to both token-settings reloads.
The signature carries service_password because the cache's
read_parties_for_cache calls need a signed JWT.
end note

note top of "ores::iam::messaging::auth_handler"
Every generated handler in this component has the same shape as the
account handler above: one method per protocol subject, each proving the
request through make_request_context, decoding the canonical request,
constructing its service for that call, and reporting a store failure as
a failed result rather than letting the exception escape.
end note

