note top of "ores::iam::messaging::register_account_history_provider"
Seven generated free functions, one per history-bearing entity, each
registering a lambda under the entity's entity_type key
("ores.iam.account" and so on). The lambda constructs the entity's
service on the scoped request context, reads the full history vector,
and turns it into versions with ores.history's
build_entity_history_versions and the entity's presentation renderer, so
the generic history.v1.get subject serves every IAM entity without one
subject per entity.
end note

